      "text": "Given that \\(a = 3b\\), \\(b = 2c\\), and \\(c = 4d\\), we need to find the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\(b = 2c\\) into the equation \\(a = 3b\\):\n\\[\na = 3(2c) = 6c\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(c = 4d\\) into the equation \\(a = 6c\\):\n\\[\na = 6(4d) = 24d\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(b = 2c\\) and \\(c = 4d\\) into the expression \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d} = \\frac{24d \\cdot 4d}{2c \\cdot d}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\\[\n24d \\cdot 4d = 96d^2\n\\]\n\nSimplify the denominator:\n\\[\n2c \\cdot d = 2(4d) \\cdot d = 8d^2\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{96d^2}{8d^2}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{96d^2}{8d^2} = 12\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{a \\cdot c}{b \\cdot d}\\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
